            "lang": "en",
            "supportingMedia": [
              {
                "base64": false,
                "type": "text/html",
                "value": "<span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">A malicious TLS1.2 server can force a TLS1.3 client with downgrade capability to use a ciphersuite that it did not agree to and achieve a successful connection. This is because, aside from the extensions, the client was skipping fully parsing the server hello.</span><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.46586/tches.v2024.i1.457-500\"></a><br>"
              }
            ],
            "value": "A malicious TLS1.2 server can force a TLS1.3 client with downgrade capability to use a ciphersuite that it did not agree to and achieve a successful connection. This is because, aside from the extensions, the client was skipping fully parsing the server hello.  https://doi.org/10.46586/tches.v2024.i1.457-500"
          }
        ],
